WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
 I'll say it again, so proud of the city that I love, the city that we love.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.000
 I mentioned the Good Stuff family, the stories that we're trying to tell now.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
 We stand up two things. We say, "Together we can, together we will, and God weaves,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.000
 now watch and work."

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
 And that's what I'm saying here. I'm in awe, again, of all of the Good Stuff

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
 that is at the core of the heart of the city that we love.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:34.110
 Okay, next up we have May Chen, inducted by Margaret Wong. Margaret Wong was

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.000
 inducted into the inaugural class of the CIHF.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.150
 She's the leading immigration attorney in the country and has been a strong and

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:46.000
 generous supporter of most cultural and ethnic activities in the city.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.000
 We follow Mr. Redna and Valerie, both old, old friends.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.270
 And before I introduce May Chen, I want to tell everybody in this room that Mr.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:08.000
 Redna and my family and girls and sister and I, we go way, way back.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.220
 When I first moved to Cleveland, I was young, I was hungry, I was an absent

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:13.000
 nobody.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.680
 We didn't even have $200 in effect. I went through a horrible personal

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.000
 relationship.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.000
 And the first person I met was the person named Albert Redna. He was so humble.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.470
 I didn't know he was that rich, and the daughter was the rich and now, but the

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:30.000
 most righteous person in his home.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.140
 So he came, he said hello, and Rose, the pearl of the Orion restaurant, has

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.000
 been this kind of, since day one, we are there.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.680
 So we talked about when the new mall started and the family, Redna family,

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.000
 again, is on the board.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:52.060
 And we are closing on June 30th. So Mr. Redna gave Rose an awesome, awesome

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.000
 send-off.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.000
 He has helped my family so much, so much, so much.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.490
 And I was a young lawyer, he referred clients, he would come to the restaurant

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:06.130
 at night and say, this is how you do things, this is what you do, you know, and

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.000
 don't worry about it.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.060
 And my reputation is, time goes on, we're talking about, you know, the old, the

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:15.000
 Nazi people, and of course, his tuition.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.970
 And he'll tell me, don't you ever dare, what can I do? I mean, I do know, but

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.000
 you know, we don't.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.000
 So I just cannot thank you. And I had some struggles.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.440
 The plane dealer was the, my little, my little, my little friend Alex Atreskys

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.230
 here, they had such bad complaints about me and my racism, and of course, I was

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.000
 too good.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.840
 So who called me the first time? Like, when Rose came to see me at home, Mr.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.000
 Redna gave me, he said, don't worry about the plane dealer.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.000
 You go on, you do this, you do that, and I came back up.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.180
 We have nine offices now, and I want to thank you. And I've set some horrible

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:57.000
 things, and I say wrong things, he'll call me and say, I heard you said this,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.000
 don't you ever.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.000
 You are a somebody now. You're no longer 30 years ago who you were.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:10.820
 So Mr. Redna, I owe you big, big time, even now, to call us, I won't zero-beam,

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:15.000
 my husband and I, you are awesome. And personally, that's such a big question.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:21.640
 But of course, as an old-fashioned Chinese with an old Jewish, I do this, I do

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.000
 this, I do everything.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:34.240
 Oh my gosh, is he this? Is he that? My husband knows all that. So now let's

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.000
 talk about it. We have to do better than Mr. Redna, not this competition.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.000
 Come, clap for me.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.000
 [Applause]

00:03:43.000 --> 00:04:08.000
 [Applause]

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:32.000
 [Applause]

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.950
 What a great honor it is for me to receive the Cleveland International Hall of

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:40.440
 Fame Award. I do want to thank profusely, Mark R

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.340
 Wong and the Cleveland International Hall of Fame Selection Committee for this

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:52.430
 honor. At the Tenement Museum in New York City, there's a poll. People without

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.000
 ambitions stay home.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:01.060
 Only those with ambition were willing to risk their lives and fortunes, travel

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:06.000
 long distances, and attempt a new life in the United States.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:12.000
 I believe this prestigious award should rightfully be shared with these people,

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:18.000
 immigrants and refugees, whom I have the honor and privilege of helping and

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.000
 serving.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:25.460
 I'm constantly humbled and moved by their matchless resiliency, great

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:32.150
 sacrifices, endurance of unspeakable pain, and remarkable adjustment to

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:38.330
 challenging circumstances in this country, in order to realize their hopes and

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:41.000
 dreams for themselves and them.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:46.850
 My work was simply to do the right and just thing. By advocating on their

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:53.470
 behalf, helping them navigate through unfamiliar terrain to overcome barriers

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:56.000
 here and to reach their goals.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:03.000
 My journey with them has been fulfilling, inspiring, and great joy.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:08.610
 In the early 30s, when my parents came to study in America, they were inspired

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:14.360
 by their thought provoking professors, witnessed boundless opportunities to

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:20.280
 create and succeed, and felt much warmth and support from fellow Americans

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.000
 during their stay.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:28.260
 After returning to China and Hong Kong, they were convinced America was the

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:34.220
 place where their children would thrive and succeed. My siblings and I will

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:39.000
 forever remain grateful for the sacrifices they made for us coming to America.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:44.880
 My choice of profession to help and serve immigrants and refugees would not

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:51.110
 come to fruition were it not for this country's great heart, for the displays,

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:54.000
 oppressed, and marginalized.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:00.250
 Service, compassion, generosity, and human rights characterize the strength of

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:05.980
 this country. Therefore, I will remain always grateful to this country for

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:11.990
 realizing my dream to improve the quality of life for immigrants and refugees,

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:17.000
 to become fully contributing and patriotic American citizens.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:22.490
 Joining me tonight are many who encourage and support and advocate for my

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:24.000
 community work.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:31.000
 Asia CEO Elayto and her leadership team and Asia board members.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:38.230
 Cleveland Community leaders, Annie Hu of the Erie Journal, Anna Lee, President

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:45.600
 of the Chinese Women's Association, Chia Chen, City of Cleveland Community

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:51.000
 Relations, and Dr. Kevin Hartley from East Western University.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:56.000
 I want to thank my husband, Dr. C.F. Chen, for bringing me to North East Ohio,

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:04.000
 where we work, where we raise the family, and we're able to serve the community.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:10.080
 And also I want to thank my children and grandchildren for supporting Asia all

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.000
 these years since they were born.

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:19.980
 My fervent hope is that we must continue to work together to foster and nurture

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:27.510
 women, men, young adults, youth in our immigrant and refugee community, to be

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:30.000
 meaningful voices and leaders.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:36.050
 North East Ohio can provide the resources and opportunities to realize this

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:38.000
 most important goal.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.000
 Our own immigrant communities must commit to be civically engaged.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:48.840
 We must find time and learn to incorporate altruism, compassion, and

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.000
 philanthropy in our daily living.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:59.070
 Finally, during these difficult times from the pandemic, racism, and political

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:05.970
 divide, we must re-establish our faith in one another, revert to our country's

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:07.000
 core values,

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:13.050
 and continue to welcome immigrants and refugees who hold great promise and

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:16.000
 growth and strength for America.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:17.000
 Thank you.

